---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Private Voice-Activated Teleprompter | teleprompter.wtf';
const description =
  'How Smart Pace and Private Precision Beta follow your voice locally without sending scripts, microphone audio, or recognition fragments to a server.';
const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'Private voice tracking for a browser teleprompter',
    description,
    datePublished: '2026-08-09',
    dateModified: '2026-08-09',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'teleprompter.wtf' },
    mainEntityOfPage: 'https://www.teleprompter.wtf/private-voice-tracking',
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://www.teleprompter.wtf/' },
      {
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: 2,
        name: 'Private voice tracking',
        item: 'https://www.teleprompter.wtf/private-voice-tracking',
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} ogType="article" schema={schema}>
  <article class="prose-page section-wrap">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">Private voice tracking</span>
    </nav>
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Voice that stays local</p>
      <h1>A teleprompter can follow you without a speech server.</h1>
      <p>
        Manual, Smart Pace, and Private Precision Beta offer three levels of control. None sends
        your script or microphone audio to teleprompter.wtf.
      </p>
      <a class="button button--primary" href="/">Try the teleprompter</a>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-body prose-body--wide">
      <h2>Manual is the foundation</h2>
      <p>
        Manual uses a steady, elapsed-time scroll with an adjustable speed. It never requests the
        microphone and keeps working when every advanced browser capability is unavailable.
      </p>
      <h2>Smart Pace follows rhythm, not words</h2>
      <p>
        Smart Pace samples the local microphone signal through Web Audio. It calibrates to the room,
        estimates speech activity, smooths cadence changes, and gradually stops during a meaningful
        pause. It does not turn speech into text, needs no download, and works in any language. It
        is the recommended default for most setups.
      </p>
      <h2>Private Precision Beta follows your place</h2>
      <p>
        Private Precision Beta downloads a quantized multilingual Whisper Tiny model from this site.
        A browser worker recognizes short audio windows locally, then a deterministic alignment
        engine compares the temporary fragment with a bounded region of the script. High-confidence
        matches gently correct position. Low-confidence matches fall back to Smart Pace.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is still in beta, and results can differ across devices, accents, and environments. There
        is no cloud speech processing and no script or audio upload: everything the model hears
        stays on this device. If it does not track well in your setting, Smart Pace and Manual
        remain available.
      </p>
      <div class="privacy-flow" aria-label="Private Precision Beta processing flow">
        <span>Microphone</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Local model</span><b
          aria-hidden="true">→</b
        ><span>Temporary fragment</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b><span>Local alignment</span><b
          aria-hidden="true">→</b
        ><span>Smooth correction</span>
      </div>
      <h2>The model download</h2>
      <p>
        The local model and its runtime total about 67 MB on first download. Nothing downloads on
        the normal homepage or when presenter mode opens. Download begins only after you select
        Private Precision Beta and press the download button. The versioned files are kept in this
        browser and can be removed from the same panel or the privacy page.
      </p>
      <h2>What is temporary</h2>
      <p>
        Microphone samples and recognition fragments exist only while voice tracking is active. They
        are not written to local storage, IndexedDB, URLs, analytics, diagnostics, or application
        logs. Closing the presenter stops media tracks and disposes of the worker.
      </p>
      <h2>Browser and device differences</h2>
      <p>
        Smart Pace needs microphone access and Web Audio. Private Precision Beta also needs
        WebAssembly, a Worker, storage space, and enough memory for local inference. The interface
        reports a coarse device recommendation, but initialization success is the final capability
        check. When precision cannot start, Manual and Smart Pace remain available.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a practical comparison of voice-follow methods, read <a
          href="/guides/voice-activated-teleprompters">the voice-activated teleprompter guide</a
        >. For the complete data boundary, see the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
